1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:08,010
-r sets a frame rate.

2
00:00:08,010 --> 00:00:18,380
Before -i or after -i: same thing?

3
00:00:18,380 --> 00:00:26,910
Source: 60 frames, 30 fps, 2.0 s.

4
00:00:26,910 --> 00:00:35,440
Two readers: ffprobe, and what is inside.

5
00:00:35,440 --> 00:00:42,460
-r 10 after -i: 22 frames, 2.2 s.

6
00:00:42,460 --> 00:00:47,730
fps=10 filter: 20 frames, 2.0 s.

7
00:00:47,730 --> 00:00:56,130
-r 10 before -i: all 60 frames kept.

8
00:00:56,130 --> 00:01:03,480
Plays 6 s, at one third speed.

9
00:01:03,480 --> 00:01:08,220
-r 10 before -i, with -c copy:

10
00:01:08,220 --> 00:01:12,290
no effect. 30 fps, 2.0 s.

11
00:01:12,290 --> 00:01:18,890
Raw H.264: default 30 fps, 2 s.

12
00:01:18,890 --> 00:01:26,430
-r 10 before -i: 10 fps, 6 s.

13
00:01:26,430 --> 00:01:35,230
After -i: changes the frames.

14
00:01:35,230 --> 00:01:44,040
Before -i: changes the clock.
